TITLE:: SequencerDocument
SUMMARY:: Encapsulates reading and writing sequencer source in a Document.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/Document, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/WriteCommand, Classes/PatternText

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: composes a LINK::Classes/Document:: and is the place that knows how sequencer source is laid out: how to find MIDI parts, where to write new pattern text, and (later) how to parse or replace existing sequences.

LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::, LINK::Classes/SequencerGui::, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand:: talk to this class rather than to LINK::Classes/Document:: directly. Callers of LINK::#-insertPattern:: do not choose the insertion point; TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: owns that policy.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: wrapping the given LINK::Classes/Document::.

ARGUMENT:: document
The LINK::Classes/Document:: that holds sequencer source (typically LINK::Classes/Document#*current:: when the GUI opens).

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SequencerDocument:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: insertPattern
Inserts pattern source into the composed LINK::Classes/Document::. The insertion location is chosen by TELETYPE::SequencerDocument::; callers do not specify it.

ARGUMENT:: string
The pattern source text to insert.

RETURNS::
This instance.

PRIVATE:: init, prIndexForInsert, prIsWhitespace
